  "notes": "{恥|は}ずかしがる is a godan verb formed from the adjective {恥|は}ずかしい (embarrassed) + the suffix がる.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし})\n- Pattern: Xが{恥|は}ずかしがる\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{恥|は}ずかしがっている describes someone visibly showing shyness or embarrassment at the moment.\n\nThe がる suffix converts adjectives (typically い-adjectives) into verbs that describe observable behavior, particularly useful for describing third-person emotions:\n- {恥|は}ずかしい (I feel embarrassed) → {恥|は}ずかしがる (to show embarrassment - third person)\n- {欲|ほ}しい (I want) → {欲|ほ}しがる (to show wanting)\n- {寂|さび}しい (I'm lonely) → {寂|さび}しがる (to show loneliness)",
